bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed family of supplied lattice values, associative and commutative meet is independent of their arrival permutation. This does not erase effective epochs, widening, withdrawals or the order of equal-epoch acts." at=policy:law/A2 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A2-meet.json|samples/no/A2-meet.json|vectors/meet.json|vectors/join.json|vectors/fold.json|test/knowledge-laws-042.test.ts role=demands scope=law/A2-meet value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="every observation has a scale; hierarchy is resolution; a coordinate's depth is its resolution" at=policy:law/A3 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A3-resolution.json|samples/no/A3-resolution.json|vectors/field.json|vectors/render.json role=demands scope=law/A3-resolution value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="every claim carries when it holds; order is causal, never a clock" at=policy:law/A4 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A4-epoch.json|samples/no/A4-epoch.json|vectors/info/observation-close.json role=demands scope=law/A4-epoch value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Declared extensional convention: an origin is identified by its supplied set of coordinate/interval pairs. Equal extensions form one class. Distance between extensions is descriptive; it does not establish probabilistic independence." at=policy:law/A5 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A5-origin-is-extension.json|samples/no/A5-origin-is-extension.json|vectors/atom/states-not-actions.json role=demands scope=law/A5-origin-is-extension value=present view=galois
