bound-lock/1 about="one origin is required; two or more that meet within the ceiling are free; that meet outside it are forbidden; that do not meet are in conflict; fewer states collapse two of them" at=policy:law/A8 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A8-four-states.json|samples/no/A8-four-states.json role=demands scope=law/A8-four-states value=present view=ideal
bound-lock/1 about="one relation: an origin bounds a cell at a resolution and an epoch; cells, origins, locks and laws are cells under it; the relation bounds itself, and there is no level above it" at=policy:law/A9 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A9-everything-is-a-bound.json|samples/no/A9-everything-is-a-bound.json role=demands scope=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="For fixed coordinates, resolution, context and signed ceilings, adding live narrowing claims cannot increase the sum of log-cardinalities of finite admissible states. Exact withdrawal and witnessed local widening may reopen freedom at the same coordinate. The blanket exclusivity claim that only a new coordinate raises freedom is not valid. Historical alias: freedom-conserved." at=policy:law/A7 by=target form=alphabet kind=axiom measure=status needs=samples/yes/A7-freedom-conserved.json|samples/no/A7-freedom-conserved.json|test/laws-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a7-t90.json role=demands scope=law/A7-freedom-conserved value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="a coordinate exists where two origins agree they observe one thing; the coordinate set of a domain is the fold of recognitions, never a schema" at=policy:law/D0 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D0-coordinate.json|vectors/info/falsifier.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/D0-coordinate value=present view=field
