bound-lock/1 about="Under uniform truth and an independent covering-cause indicator of mass c, active observations copy one n-ary symmetric channel of accuracy q; I(truth;observations) <= log2(n)-c*(h(q)+(1-q)*log2(n-1)); copies add no information. Historical alias: reliability-is-encounter-rate. No achievability or partial governance claim." at=policy:law/T12 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/measures/t12/common-cause.json|vectors/measures/t12/expected.json role=demands scope=law/T12-reliability-is-encounter-rate value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="an independent second origin never raises a cell's debit: it falls by log2 of the states it leaves standing, a full bit exactly when it admits at most half of them, and nothing exactly when it narrows nothing" at=policy:law/T16 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T16-encounter-inequality.json|samples/no/T16-encounter-inequality.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/T14-supermodular-degeneration role=demands scope=law/T16-encounter-inequality value=present view=chain
