bound-lock/1 about="In a common probability space with justified declared failure upper bounds p_i, the probability of all declared events succeeding is at least max(0,1-sum(p_i)); sum(p_i)>=1 is trivial. Agreement and copy counts do not estimate probabilities. Historical alias: freedom-is-a-currency; no transferability or unforgeability claim." at=policy:law/T18 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/measures/confidence/union-bound.json|vectors/measures/confidence/expected.json role=demands scope=law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed supplied collection of signed bounds with declared polarity and lattice form, foldSigned retains the extensional classes and evaluates their form operations; meet of fixed permit values is associative and commutative. This static fold is not a claim that chronological withdrawal, replacement or witnessed widening can never occur." at=policy:law/T19 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T19-signatures-fold.json|vectors/signatures.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/D7-fork role=demands scope=law/T19-signatures-fold value=present view=lattice
