bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. n origins on a cell agree at a resolution; raising it opens agreements into forks, each a coordinate the coarser scale hid; the sufficient resolution of a region is where its residual figure stops changing" at=policy:law/T36 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution.json|test/loom.test.ts restsOn=law/A3-resolution|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree|law/T7-sufficient-resolution role=demands scope=law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="For finite held real intervals and lock intervals with strictly positive finite width, stretching about each fixed midpoint eventually contains every bounded nonempty held interval; an empty held interval is never accepted by red. pour counts reached named lock places. tense interpolates touched inhabited endpoints toward their held endpoints at a handed rate in [0,1]; touching narrows width only when the held interval is no wider, and may widen it otherwise. Missing or empty observations use the specified widening rule. The historical seeded deformation counts are experiments, not a physical adaptation law." at=policy:law/T37 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould.json|src/views/product/mould.ts|test/loom.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould value=present view=dual
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite nonempty family of nonempty closed real intervals, pairwise nonempty intersection implies a nonempty total intersection. The lattice interval form supplies this finite Helly-2 case; no polygon/consensus claim for arbitrary forms. Convex families in R^d require Helly hypotheses and d+1 witnesses; discrete circle and halfplane fixtures distinguish pairs from triples. Historical alias: origins-are-a-polygon." at=policy:law/T38 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/laws/t38/intervals.json|vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T38-origins-are-a-polygon value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="the independence of two origins is the distance between their extensions: one extension is one origin, disjoint extensions share nothing" at=policy:law/C1 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/C1-independence-is-distance.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/C1-independence-is-distance value=present view=galois
