bound-lock/1 about="Data processing forces submodularity — Every valuation with the data-processing property is submodular. Among such valuations, $g\\equiv0$ if and only if $f$ is modular." at=policy:law/C4 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=vectors/hypothesis.json restsOn=law/thm-collapse|law/thm-modular role=demands scope=law/C4-dpi-subadditive value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="where reading already is, the next reading lands: over eight epochs of placement in proportion to the origins a cell already carries, the ratio between the densest tenth and the sparsest rises at every epoch and the deserts stay empty, while the same budget placed blind to density holds that ratio near two and touches three times as many cells" at=policy:law/H2 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H2-density-attracts.json|samples/no/H2-density-attracts.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/H2-density-attracts value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="For finite distinct real walls and finite distinct sites strictly inside their bounding consecutive-wall intervals, grow assigns each site the interval between its wall or nearest-site midpoints. Adding another distinct interior site while retaining the walls cannot increase an existing site width: its left endpoint can only increase and its right endpoint can only decrease. No encounter, sufficient-resolution or general-form growth law follows; wall-coincident, duplicate, nonfinite and out-of-domain sites are outside this claim." at=policy:law/T39 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped.json|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier role=demands scope=law/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the declared finite graph/placement fixtures; general placement/valuation interpretation open. T18 now states a conditional union bound and supplies no currency or placement proof. what knowing costs is not set by how many origins look but by where they land: one budget of two hundred gives a ratio near two placed blind and above twenty placed where reading already is, so the shape of what is known is a fact about placement, and it leaves cities and deserts in one field" at=policy:law/T40 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T40-cost-by-density.json restsOn=law/T38-origins-are-a-polygon|law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked|law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency role=demands scope=law/T40-cost-by-density value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="For a fixed nonempty finite world with unique coordinates, neighbours forms the undirected graph of shared supplied origins, excluding explicitly named bounds. On each connected component distance is shortest-path length: reversing paths proves symmetry, concatenating paths proves the triangle inequality, and zero length identifies one vertex. Breadth-first layers return the minimum path length. The implementation returns world.length as the top sentinel for an unreachable pair; it is not an observed travel length. Sample means and any physical interpretation remain experiments." at=policy:law/T41 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings.json|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Two readings with identical complete live claims, values, form, resolution, epoch/effective ordering and required world/mark context return the same deterministic meet and verdict. For the published point fixture, identical full seen records give identical potential/disagreement verdicts. Equal origin names alone do not ensure equal readings; claims and context may differ. The seeded observer counts are finite experiments; no universal horizon-only explanation of disagreement is asserted." at=policy:law/T42 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T42-no-privileged-observer.json|src/field/encounter.ts|src/field/meet.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/A4-epoch role=demands scope=law/T42-no-privileged-observer value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="information and distance are two readings of one thing: with no origin there is neither a fact nor a finite distance, and each origin that lands gives exactly one of each" at=policy:law/T43 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T43-each-origin-gives-one-fact-and-one-distance.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/T43-each-origin-gives-one-fact-and-one-distance value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the declared finite graph/placement fixtures; general placement/valuation interpretation open. T18 now states a conditional union bound and supplies no currency or placement proof. one claim of one width is worth what it connects: nothing inside a city where every pair already had a walk, one pair between two lone cells, and the product of two components when it lands across a desert, so where to look is a question with an answer and the answer is read before the claim lands" at=policy:law/T44 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach.json restsOn=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked|law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. cells that rest on one bound move together when it moves: narrowing a ceiling turns cells red with nobody looking at them, some past the horizon of whoever signed it, and the effect is the bound's and not the order's, since the same narrowing taken in two steps names exactly the cells it names in one" at=policy:law/T45 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled.json|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T19-signatures-fold|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings role=demands scope=law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. a world changes in two ways at once: looking travels and stops at the horizon, a bound does not travel and carries no step, so moving it changes cells no walk reaches; counting the bound as if it were a looking would make the whole world one neighbourhood, which is how the two are told apart" at=policy:law/T46 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches.json|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. one coordinate on a scale of a hundred and five levels is superposed at six point seven bits, definite when two claims meet at one level, and forbidden rather than narrow when a ceiling falls under that floor, while a second coordinate resting on the bound that moved narrows to five point four bits with nobody measuring it" at=policy:law/T47 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T47-a-two-pole-object.json|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled|law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches role=demands scope=law/T47-a-two-pole-object value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. an epoch is a phase: claims arriving at one turn of a period reinforce and claims half a period apart cancel, so sweeping the delay of half of them draws the period's own shape, and observing one route, which is fixing when those claims arrived, moves the pattern to its complement" at=policy:law/T48 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T48-epoch-is-phase.json|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/T22-fold-is-superposition|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/T48-epoch-is-phase value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the explicitly supplied finite sample. The historical descriptive text below is not a universal or physical theorem; general extrapolation remains open. a claim carries a size and a direction, how much it narrows and the turn it landed on, and a withdrawal is the same size the other way: two hundred claims in phase make the square of their number and the same two hundred strewn make its order, while a write and its withdrawal at one epoch leave nothing and at different epochs do not cancel" at=policy:law/T49 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase.json|samples/no/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase.json|test/wave.test.ts restsOn=law/T48-epoch-is-phase|law/T19-signatures-fold|law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment, one-origin structural interpretation; general/physical-law reading open. stated as a hint and never as a claim about the world: if what is is a field of floors and ceilings, a distant signature changes a cell whose own record never moved, and in two hundred trials of one cell holding one value the verdict came out both ways, so nothing stored at the cell explains the difference and what explains it is the bound the cell rests on; the resemblance is structural and never arithmetic, with no continuous amplitudes and no inequality violated by number; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H3 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json|samples/no/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json restsOn=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches|law/T47-a-two-pole-object role=demands scope=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="the object is c = ⟨⊥, ⊤, O, ⊑⟩ over L at r: four parts in two pairs, the value (⊥, ⊤) and the relations (O, ⊑), with the lattice L it is given and the resolution r it is read at belonging to the reading and the sign to the act; an origin is (o, φ), and the poles are read, never stored: ⊥ is what is required joined with what its live claims hold, ⊤ what is signed met with what they allow; eight acts in four pairs and seven names answer for it: meet and join on the ceiling, local, a join only with a witness; observe and withdraw on the floor, local, a withdrawal being an observation at −1 that restores exactly; sign and require on both poles, travelling by rest, commuting and both closing freedom; encounter and refine with no pole; and no widening travels" at=policy:law/D11 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/obligatory.json|samples/no/obligatory.json|vectors/moves.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/A2-meet|law/A4-epoch|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound role=demands scope=law/D11-the-obligatory value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a signature narrows a ceiling and travels to every cell that rests on it as a meet, and meets do not remember the order they were taken in, so no order of any number of signatures ever shows in the field they leave; widening is not a meet and does not travel, which is why a narrowing costs one signature and an error costs one at every cell, and folding the field and signing it commute even with a withdrawal present" at=policy:law/T50 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T50-signatures-are-meets.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T19-signatures-fold role=demands scope=law/T50-signatures-are-meets value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="In a finite undirected graph with distinct named vertices, positive component sizes and unrestricted unit-cost fresh bridges that join only their two chosen components, a nonnegative integer budget b minimises unreachable unordered pairs by connecting the min(b+1,k) largest of k components into one. The objective is (N^2-sum(componentSize^2))/2; arbitrary site restrictions, nonuniform costs and origin-name collisions are outside this theorem. design returns a star on representatives of those components. Historical comparisons against particular blind seeds remain experiments, not universal superiority over every competing draw." at=policy:law/T51 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed.json|src/views/product/design.ts|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment in the declared finite cities/lone-cell fixtures, budgets, epochs and random seeds. evolve uses the handed attachment sampling rule; loom repeatedly uses the graph design over the resulting field. The recorded undirected runs leave a horizon after sixty epochs and the recorded directed run closes it at the specified step. General autonomous concentration, universal convergence under arbitrary policies and resource costs remain open; no vacuity dynamics or assertion about a self-governing machine follows from these observations." at=policy:law/T52 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T52-directing-where-origins-land-closes-the-horizon.json|src/views/field/physics.ts|src/views/product/design.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed role=demands scope=law/T52-directing-where-origins-land-closes-the-horizon value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="the cells under the order of rest, with signatures as meets and the phase each origin carries as what they are enriched over, look like an enriched meet-semilattice, and what this library proves would be its representation theory; identity, composition, associativity, commuting and naturality hold for the operations as vectors, while observation is not one of them — it moves the metric and can split a cell no signature could, so it is a functor out of the category and not an arrow inside it, and the join, which does not travel, is a second kind of arrow this conjecture does not name" at=policy:law/H4 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H4-enriched-semilattice.json|samples/no/H4-enriched-semilattice.json restsOn=law/T50-signatures-are-meets|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings role=demands scope=law/H4-enriched-semilattice value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment, one-origin structural interpretation; general/physical-law reading open. amplitudes with a phase and no origin, no signed ceiling, no resolution and no epoch band are what is left of a cell when those four fields are dropped, so the measurement problem is the absence of who, imposed symmetries the absence of a signed ceiling, the classical limit the absence of resolution and universal interference the absence of bands; restored, four claims in phase keep exactly the share of the whole their number leaves them against an environment spread over the period, and six origins around one value are six objects read finely and one read coarsely, so how many things there are is a reading; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H5 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json|samples/no/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json restsOn=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a lock is mostly settled: the form of most claims leaves them one legal state and they are applied, what the form leaves wider splits into those a reading has closed and those standing in force with nothing read against them, and the few that say of themselves that they are decisions are the only ones open; the four classes are a partition, every claim in exactly one, and a decision is not a claim with a wide ceiling but a claim that declares itself unanswered" at=policy:law/T53 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T53-a-decision-is-what-the-form-leaves-open.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A8-four-states|law/D3-state|law/T26-knowing-has-four-states role=demands scope=law/T53-a-decision-is-what-the-form-leaves-open value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment for the named historical tree: 2453 leaves and 309 declared regions. Region membership is prefix containment and may have zero, one or many observed leaves. There is no universal leaves-greater-than-regions inequality or cost-independent-of-atom-count conclusion: an observed region plus an empty region with only one observed leaf falsifies that cardinality implication. Reading-cost scaling requires a separate declared reader/work model and remains open." at=policy:law/T58 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T58-observation-is-over-regions-by-reach.json|src/field/field.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A3-resolution|law/D1-region role=demands scope=law/T58-observation-is-over-regions-by-reach value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment for the declared finite field, weights, seed, draw, spread and look budget. choose scores current reach, coherence at period 8, graph degree and log2(1+held width) under the handed four weights; play counts its specified closing/fork/coverage events. The recorded mixed weights outperform the recorded specialist weights on that fixture. Universal dominance for all fields, weights, draws or objectives is open and is not implied by component-bridge optimisation." at=policy:law/T55 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights.json|src/views/field/policy.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts|src/views/product/reach.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/D11-the-obligatory|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase role=demands scope=law/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Research status: experiment for the three declared spread regimes under the same finite seeded play procedure and mixed weights. The test compares forks/max(1,closed), including a denominator guard, and obtains distinct recorded ratios. This is a descriptive fixture statistic, not a universal regime classifier or a finite forks/closed ratio when closed=0. General interpretation, objective and uncertainty remain open." at=policy:law/T56 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T56-forks-over-closes-separates-regimes.json|src/views/field/policy.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights role=demands scope=law/T56-forks-over-closes-separates-regimes value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="For the existing object state reading with fewer than two distinct live origin names, the cell cannot be FREE: incompatible required/signed constraints give CONFLICT first, otherwise the origin-count branch gives REQUIRED. Further claims of the same origin do not increase that distinct-name count. The seeded twenty-cell play results are experiments; player permissions, identity authenticity, independence, asymmetric economic value and an unsuspendable referee are not consequences of this state rule and remain open." at=policy:law/T57 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself.json|src/lattice/obligatory.ts|src/field/encounter.ts|src/views/field/policy.ts|test/obligatory.test.ts restsOn=law/A8-four-states|law/D11-the-obligatory role=demands scope=law/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="who said it, when they said it and what is remembered are three coordinates of one claim and none of them is the claim: two origins saying one span are two claims and one origin saying it twice is one, so what a cell holds together depends on the spans alone while what it is depends on all three" at=policy:law/T63 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T63-author-time-memory-are-relative.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/D0-coordinate|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree role=demands scope=law/T63-author-time-memory-are-relative value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="to own a claim is to be the origin of it and nothing else: a cell holds what each origin said, taking an origin away takes exactly what it said and no more, and no narrowing survives the origin that made it" at=policy:law/T65 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T65-ownership-is-being-an-origin.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A1-encounter|law/D5-declaration|law/T8-exact-withdrawal role=demands scope=law/T65-ownership-is-being-an-origin value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="there is no after: what stands at a cell is what the latest epoch says and the order the claims arrived in never decides, so every order of one set of claims leaves one reading and a clock is not a fact about the field" at=policy:law/T66 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T66-there-is-no-after.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/T22-fold-is-superposition|law/T50-signatures-are-meets|law/D8-present role=demands scope=law/T66-there-is-no-after value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a withdrawal takes back what a claim did and never that it was made: the claim stays on the cell, the origin still spoke, and what changed is what the cell now means, which is why a withdrawal is a reinterpretation and not an erasure" at=policy:law/T67 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T67-withdrawal-is-reinterpretation.json restsOn=law/T8-exact-withdrawal|law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter|law/T19-signatures-fold role=demands scope=law/T67-withdrawal-is-reinterpretation value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a gap is not the absence of a claim but a claim at the coarsest resolution: a cell nobody has narrowed holds the whole scale, which is exactly what saying nothing says, so a reading that is missing and a reading that allows everything are one line and a tree with gaps is a tree read coarsely" at=policy:law/T70 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T70-a-gap-is-a-coarse-claim.json restsOn=law/A6-vacuity|law/A3-resolution|law/D1-region|law/T5-coarsen-widens role=demands scope=law/T70-a-gap-is-a-coarse-claim value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="four instruments that share no mechanism fold the same way because a measurement is a cell: for a thermometer, a survey, an interferometer and a headcount the five fields are named without strain and the same five operations answer for all four; no number is claimed, only that the table can be filled in every row" at=policy:law/H6 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H6-structure-of-measurement.json|samples/no/H6-structure-of-measurement.json restsOn=law/D11-the-obligatory|law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/H6-structure-of-measurement value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="what carries an encounter is a medium, and a medium is what two origins can both reach: in each instrument the medium can be named and the encounter happens where two origins touch it and nowhere else, so two origins at one cell make information and the same two at two cells make none; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H7 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H7-the-medium-of-encounters.json|samples/no/H7-the-medium-of-encounters.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/D1-region role=demands scope=law/H7-the-medium-of-encounters value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a field of cells with origins and signatures is a game whose referee is inside it: a move is a claim, a claim alone is potential, two that meet are information, a signature moves every cell that rests on it, and no player may suspend the rule that makes the first four; the claim is that each of five readings of the field matches all five properties; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H8 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H8-refereed-game.json|samples/no/H8-refereed-game.json restsOn=law/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself|law/A1-encounter|law/T50-signatures-are-meets role=demands scope=law/H8-refereed-game value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a cell that folds itself converges: observing each epoch a claim of width ten centred on its own meet and off by at most s, it narrows only when the offset cuts inside what it holds, so its freedom settles toward log2(11 − 2s) from above and it never conflicts; at s = 3, sixty epochs leave it between 2.38 and 2.43 bits on three seeds" at=policy:law/T73 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T73-a-cell-that-folds-itself-converges.json restsOn=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T73-a-cell-that-folds-itself-converges value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="the obligatory is maximal: take away any one of its seven parts and what is left is an object already known, and anything added to it is either already inside it or breaks the four states" at=policy:law/H9 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal.json|samples/no/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal.json restsOn=law/A8-four-states|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/D11-the-obligatory role=demands scope=law/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A2-meet/formula value="meet(c) = ⊤ ∧ ⋀_{o∈O} span_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A1-encounter/formula value="info(c) ⟺ |ext(O)| ≥ 2 ∧ meet(c) ≠ ∅"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D4-debit-in-bits/formula value="F(c) = log₂ |{x ∈ L : ⊥ ≤ x ≤ ⊤}|"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T50-signatures-are-meets/formula value="sign: ⊤(c′) ← ⊤(c′) ∧ s   ∀ c′ ⊒ c"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D11-the-obligatory/floor value="⊥(c) = ⋁ required ∨ ⋁_{o∈O} lo_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D11-the-obligatory/ceiling value="⊤(c) = ⋀ signed ∧ ⋀_{o∈O} hi_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A8-four-states/formula value="state(c) ∈ {FREE, REQUIRED, FORBIDDEN, CONFLICT}"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A0-carrier/formula value="x ⊨ c ⟺ ⊥ ⊑ x ⊑ ⊤"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A4-epoch/formula value="claim = (o, span, e), e ≺ e′ ⟺ e → e′"
