bound-lock/1 about="Bounded object contract: with an unchanged acyclic world, well-formed unique claim ids and a withdrawal naming only the newly appended claim, observe followed by that named withdrawal restores the earlier live claims and hence its poles. The earlier state is restored, not necessarily grey. Separately, equal-magnitude opposite-signed phasors at the same phase modulo a declared positive period cancel. Epoch or causal labels alone are not phase equality. Historical alias: withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim." at=policy:law/T85 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json|samples/no/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json|src/field/observe.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="For two unit complex amplitudes with real phases, let delta=acos(cos(a-b)) in [0,pi]. Then |exp(ia)+exp(ib)|^2=2+2*cos(delta), and it is below 2 iff delta>pi/2. Raw absolute phase difference is not invariant under full turns. Laminarity, fork/close ratios and the F4 worst-case objective are not conclusions of this identity. Historical alias: the-quarter-turn." at=policy:law/T87 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T87-the-quarter-turn.json|samples/no/T87-the-quarter-turn.json|test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts|src/field/encounter.ts role=demands scope=law/T87-the-quarter-turn value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Open research interpretation; not a consequence of T87. Evenly spaced phases do not always give a forks/closes ratio of one: phases 0, 2pi/3, 4pi/3 give three cancelling pairs and zero closing pairs. General faction interpretation remains open. Historical alias: turbulence-is-factions." at=policy:law/T88 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T88-turbulence-is-factions.json|samples/no/T88-turbulence-is-factions.json restsOn=law/T87-the-quarter-turn role=demands scope=law/T88-turbulence-is-factions value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Open research hypothesis; the unit-amplitude identity in T87 proves no policy advantage. Comparing disagreement-weighted and blind policies requires a declared objective, population and sampling model. Historical alias: disagreement-is-where-to-look." at=policy:law/T89 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look.json|samples/no/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look.json restsOn=law/T87-the-quarter-turn role=demands scope=law/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite nonempty set of uniformly weighted admissible states at a fixed resolution, freedom is log2 of its cardinality, equal to its Shannon entropy. A narrowing act cannot increase this quantity. Withdrawal and witnessed local join can increase it on an existing object; phase and vacuity experiments do not establish that these are the only possible changes. Historical alias: freedom-is-entropy." at=policy:law/T90 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json|samples/no/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json|test/laws-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a7-t90.json restsOn=law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/A7-freedom-conserved role=demands scope=law/T90-freedom-is-entropy value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="many objects make a field: cells read pairwise meet or fork, the meets join them into components, and the whole can have no meet although most of its pairs do" at=policy:law/T91 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T91-many-objects-make-a-field.json|samples/no/T91-many-objects-make-a-field.json restsOn=law/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells role=demands scope=law/T91-many-objects-make-a-field value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="origins, bounds, claims and rests are cells, and the state a cell shows is the meet of its parts' states; reading deeper is reading at a finer resolution, and it converges" at=policy:law/T92 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells.json|samples/no/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells.json restsOn=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A3-resolution|law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded interval-budget contract: in a finite acyclic world with inhabited poles, finite ceiling/floor endpoints and no local widening, pay explicitly appends a travelling ceiling mark at hi-1. It refuses if hi-1<floor.lo; otherwise looksLeft decreases by one with the rest of the snapshot unchanged. The caller must explicitly charge a look; sign, observe and refine are not thereby charged automatically. Region membership is computed by the existing region predicate. No universal physical price, policy optimality or third-object claim follows. Historical alias: every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin." at=policy:law/T93 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json|samples/no/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json|src/debit/observer.ts|src/field/sign.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded diagnostic contract: on a finite acyclic rest graph with its exact reverse-edge index, bites traverses travelling non-widening ceiling marks and stops below an envelope a when meet(a,new)=a. Descendant travelling envelopes contain that ancestor meet and are also absorbed. Its cells and visits describe this diagnostic traversal. With no local widening, local-only ceiling constraints or claim spans masking these envelopes, the fixture matches changed ceilings. It proves neither actual propagation cost nor a general region-summary interval. Historical alias: a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity." at=policy:law/T94 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json|samples/no/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json|src/field/sign.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded storage/read contract: sign and require append one mark at the named cell and retain ancestor records. On finite acyclic snapshots with unique ids and no widening, poles fold applicable live local and travelling-ancestor marks and live local claims by meets; the result is independent of replay order of the same records. Withdrawing a uniquely named tighter mark exposes the meet of the remaining marks, which may include an absorbed earlier signature. One appended record is not a runtime-cost theorem: map copying and ancestry traversal are separate, and a DAG read is not bounded by depth alone. Historical alias: signatures-live-where-they-are-signed." at=policy:law/T95 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json|samples/no/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json|src/field/sign.ts|src/field/require.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="For a finite world with finite records, an acyclic dependency order and total supplied lattice operations, ancestry expansion visits each reachable name once and parts/meet perform finitely many operations. This is finite evaluation, not convergence of an arbitrary monotone-map iteration. Monotonicity alone allows a two-cycle from incomparable seeds. Every reachable dependency cycle is rejected; unreachable cycles do not affect the query. Arbitrary iterative convergence remains open without operator, seed and progress hypotheses. Historical alias: the-fold-is-total." at=policy:law/T99 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T99-the-fold-is-total.json|samples/no/T99-the-fold-is-total.json|test/fold-boundaries-042.test.ts|vectors/laws/a9-t99.json|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T99-the-fold-is-total value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Named experiment: object.test.ts simulates300 independent finite interval cells,20 explicit looks per epoch,64 states per initial cell, expiry after10 epochs and200 epochs. A running signed price ledger telescopes so freedom left plus the ledger equals its initial value; the captured fixture reports steady1200 under this scheduler. That bookkeeping identity is not Shannon entropy conservation, and the finite fixture does not prove general convergence, physical attention cost or an entropy-flow claim. Historical alias: an-act-is-paid-with-attention." at=policy:law/T100 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json|samples/no/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json|src/debit/observer.ts|test/object.test.ts role=demands scope=law/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="Bounded enumeration contract: for a finite cell history and fixed finite acyclic world with total lattice operations, fragility enumerates subsets of distinct live origin names in increasing size. For each subset it removes all history records by those names and compares both poles. It returns the smallest size changing a pole, or sentinel0 if no tested subset does. This is history-record deletion, not automatic phased cancellation; cross-origin takes can expose old records. Simultaneous-support intuition additionally assumes no cross-origin withdrawal dependencies and no masking marks. Historical alias: fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals." at=policy:law/T101 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals.json|samples/no/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals.json|src/field/fragility.ts|src/lattice/obligatory.ts restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T101-fragility-is-the-fewest-withdrawals/formula value="frag(c) = min { |W| : W ⊆ O(c), ⊥(c∖W) ≠ ⊥(c) or ⊤(c∖W) ≠ ⊤(c) }"
bound-lock/1 about="a combine of bounds meets them where they land on one cell and coarsens them where they land on many: two readers of one field fold to their meet, which neither stands beside nor forks from, and readers of several fields keep their own cells and are read together only at the region they share" at=policy:law/T102 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T102-a-combine-meets-one-cell-and-coarsens-many.json|samples/no/T102-a-combine-meets-one-cell-and-coarsens-many.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/T5-coarsen-widens role=demands scope=law/T102-a-combine-meets-one-cell-and-coarsens-many value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a reading holds at what it read, as it was when it was read: its epoch is the state of the atoms it touched, so once those atoms move the reading stays an origin of that past and says nothing of the present until it is read again; a text, a table, a schema and a tree hold their readings the same way" at=policy:law/T103 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T103-a-reading-holds-at-what-it-read.json|samples/no/T103-a-reading-holds-at-what-it-read.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/T21-reading-is-an-origin|law/D8-present role=demands scope=law/T103-a-reading-holds-at-what-it-read value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Named phase-assignment experiment: the existing fixture chooses the withdrawal epoch equal to the observation epoch when rests=false, and uses the declared withdrawal epoch when rests=true. That chosen convention yields its measured phasors, but neither-rests-on-the-other does not itself prove phase equality. A dependent withdrawal one full period later also cancels; unrelated claims assigned different phases need not. Any general concurrency-if-and-only-if-cancellation theorem requires a declared cross-clock phase-comparison rule and remains open. Historical alias: concurrent-withdrawal-cancels." at=policy:law/T104 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels.json|samples/no/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels.json|test/object.test.ts|src/views/field/wave.ts role=demands scope=law/T104-concurrent-withdrawal-cancels value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="the period a phase is read against, the one T48 and T87 turn on, is a line of the region and never a fact of the instrument: a concert, a match and a sensor-s cadence each define theirs, and two heads that read one region with its period agree on its coherence with no clock between them; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H10 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H10-the-period-is-a-line-of-the-region.json|samples/no/H10-the-period-is-a-line-of-the-region.json restsOn=law/T48-epoch-is-phase|law/T87-the-quarter-turn role=demands scope=law/H10-the-period-is-a-line-of-the-region value=present view=field
